WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.713
This is ANC One. Start with a request, then follow it all the way to the

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:11.121
finished work. We'll create an estimate, prepare a proposal, review a

00:00:11.121 --> 00:00:14.328
design, update the CRM, and check service operations.

00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:20.996
For the estimate, describe the display and the job. Here we're using a

00:00:20.996 --> 00:00:26.038
sixteen by nine foot indoor wall. The margin, contingency, and tax are

00:00:26.038 --> 00:00:30.240
stated explicitly. This is training material, not a customer quote.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:35.749
The answer includes the editable workbook, the cost breakdown, and the

00:00:35.749 --> 00:00:40.031
training sell total. It also explains the tax convention. Those assumptions

00:00:40.031 --> 00:00:43.535
stay visible instead of disappearing behind a single number.

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:49.723
Open the actual Excel file. The training summary puts the scope, rates, and

00:00:49.723 --> 00:00:53.916
assumptions together. Yellow cells identify the inputs. Scroll down to see

00:00:53.916 --> 00:00:56.966
how the direct cost becomes the selling price.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:03.101
The margin analysis carries the same figures. These are working formulas,

00:01:03.101 --> 00:01:08.036
not a flattened table. In this workbook, all two hundred eighty-nine

00:01:08.036 --> 00:01:11.176
formulas were recalculated and checked without errors.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:18.142
Stay in the same conversation and ask for the budget proposal. ANC One

00:01:18.142 --> 00:01:23.443
carries the estimate forward, with the same scope and numbers. For this

00:01:23.443 --> 00:01:26.976
example, acceptance, signatures, and sending are explicitly excluded.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.174
The finished response gives you the proposal file. The important check is

00:01:32.174 --> 00:01:36.148
that its total agrees with the estimate. Generating a document is only

00:01:36.148 --> 00:01:38.466
useful when the figures survive the handoff.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:45.542
Here is the actual proposal PDF. Review the scope, the pricing schedule, and

00:01:45.542 --> 00:01:50.061
the training assumptions. The total is two hundred twenty-four thousand,

00:01:50.061 --> 00:01:53.224
eight hundred thirty-one dollars and thirty-six cents.

00:01:54.433 --> 00:01:58.651
The specifications show the display dimensions and pixel pitch. This remains

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:03.252
a budget exercise, clearly marked training only and not for acceptance. A

00:02:03.252 --> 00:02:06.319
real proposal still needs the appropriate commercial review.

00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:11.531
For design, provide the exact words, dimensions, colors, and treatment. Here

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:16.619
the request names one main board and one ribbon. It also asks for free

00:02:16.619 --> 00:02:19.889
proofs only, with no paid final rendering or approval.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:25.440
The result is actual artwork you can open and review. Check each board

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.447
against the request, especially its dimensions and copy. A proof is a

00:02:29.447 --> 00:02:31.784
reviewable output, not an approved production delivery.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.262
Open the main-board proof and inspect the full composition. The headline,

00:02:37.262 --> 00:02:41.137
training label, and navy-and-blue treatment come from the brief. Nothing

00:02:41.137 --> 00:02:44.624
here is being presented as a real sponsor campaign.

00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:50.697
Now inspect the ribbon. A long display needs its own layout and readability

00:02:50.697 --> 00:02:54.438
check. Review the proof before approval; producing paid, native-size final

00:02:54.438 --> 00:02:56.308
files is a separate step.

00:02:57.533 --> 00:03:02.517
The CRM example starts with one clearly labelled training note, unrelated to

00:03:02.517 --> 00:03:07.917
any customer or opportunity. Ask for the record to be created, then read

00:03:07.917 --> 00:03:09.994
back. No notification is needed.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.809
A follow-up changes that same note. You don't need to identify it again.

00:03:15.809 --> 00:03:20.417
Here we update the title and add a final checklist line, leaving other

00:03:20.417 --> 00:03:21.127
records untouched.

00:03:22.333 --> 00:03:26.985
Open the CRM record itself. The updated title and the additional line are

00:03:26.985 --> 00:03:31.636
saved here, not just described in the chat. This is the difference between

00:03:31.636 --> 00:03:34.141
drafting a change and actually making one.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:39.042
The same conversation can also produce a downloadable copy. This PDF

00:03:39.042 --> 00:03:43.386
contains the verified training note and a link back to its CRM record.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:49.244
For service operations, ask for a live, read-only snapshot. This request

00:03:49.244 --> 00:03:53.888
limits the result to aggregate counts and excludes personal information. It

00:03:53.888 --> 00:03:57.687
does not create tickets, assign staff, or send messages.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.000
ANC One returns the report and a link to the Service Dashboard. The report

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.101
is an output of the live lookup, with its retrieval time recorded so you

00:04:07.101 --> 00:04:08.565
know when it was current.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:13.945
Open the one-page snapshot. Venues, events, assignments, tickets, and

00:04:13.945 --> 00:04:18.123
maintenance each have an explanation. Notice the distinction between

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:22.765
recorded assignments and fully staffed events. These numbers describe stored

00:04:22.765 --> 00:04:26.015
activity; they are not a performance score.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:31.790
Five workflows, with the outputs shown: the editable estimate, the budget

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:36.761
proposal, the design proofs, the saved CRM note, and the operations report.

00:04:36.761 --> 00:04:41.731
The lesson includes the example files so you can inspect them yourself.

00:04:42.933 --> 00:04:48.236
Start with the outcome you need. State the scope and any limits, then ask

00:04:48.236 --> 00:04:52.781
for the finished file or verified change. Review the result before sending,

00:04:52.781 --> 00:04:55.054
approving, or putting it into production.
